INT. CARTOGRAPHER'S MAP ROOM - ROYAL GEOGRAPHICAL SOCIETY - DAY - 1887

A long hall lined with oak map drawers. A skylight pours soft gray light onto a drafting table the size of a rowboat. Globes in brass frames. A smell of vellum, ink, and cold tea.

SIR RUPERT ASHBY-LOVELL (60s, silver whiskers, frock coat) stoops over the table, magnifying glass in hand. A half-finished map of the Zambezi lies pinned open.

MISS ANNELIESE BASU (30s, drafting apron, spectacles pushed up into her hair) stands at his shoulder, holding a bottle of india ink. She is the only woman in the building not carrying a tray.

On the far side of the table, MR. THADDEUS OKEKE (40s, young curator, ink stains on his cuffs, a chart tube under his arm) fidgets with a ruler.

SIR RUPERT
The river bends.

ANNELIESE
It does not.

SIR RUPERT
I have seen the sketches. It bends east.

ANNELIESE
You have seen one sketch. By a man who was never within a hundred miles.

THADDEUS
Sir Rupert, if I may.

SIR RUPERT
You may not.

ANNELIESE
He may.

SIR RUPERT
Miss Basu.

ANNELIESE
Mr. Okeke measured it himself.

THADDEUS
(unrolling the chart)
Three summers, sir. On foot. With a theodolite and a very bad mule.

Sir Rupert straightens. The magnifying glass lowers. For a moment nobody speaks. A clock ticks.

SIR RUPERT
Show me.

Thaddeus spreads the chart. The river on it runs straight, then bends west, a long soft curve. Anneliese sets the india ink beside it. Sir Rupert bends close.

SIR RUPERT (CONT'D)
That is not on my map.

ANNELIESE
No, sir.

SIR RUPERT
This will cost the Society a reprint.

THADDEUS
Seven hundred pounds.

SIR RUPERT
Seven hundred.

ANNELIESE
It is a very small sum for being right.

He eyes her. She meets his eye. A long, silent, civil duel of gazes.

SIR RUPERT
Miss Basu, you are impertinent.

ANNELIESE
Yes, sir.

SIR RUPERT
Mr. Okeke, you are insubordinate.

THADDEUS
Yes, sir.

SIR RUPERT
(softly)
You are both entirely correct.

He takes the pen from the stand and, with a hand that trembles only slightly, strikes through the old river and begins to draw the new one.
